if you're looking to stand out from the  crowd this summer just ask christian  conte and matthias copper  they belong to a group of five designers  who call themselves cowboys they make  sunglasses  from natural wood  did they come on we got the idea  traveling through central america i went  there with a friend and we went to lots  of craft markets  we saw many different ways of doing  things with wood and thought to  ourselves let's do something else  the sunglasses are modelled on design  classics and made of tropical wood  they have names like ustus ferdinand  leopold and alfonse  the designers shun thick varnish to keep  the surfaces smooth  the young entrepreneurs set up their  company in 2012 their wooden sunglasses  are sold online and at 45 dealerships  across europe prices start at 139 euros  every tree is different so every pair of  our sunglasses is unique  the feel of the materials  knows all about wooden sunglasses and  everything else that's hot this summer  she's a consultant at a cologne  opticians advising on the latest eyewear  fashions  wooden glasses aren't all that easy to  make and they're not as easy to fit as  plastic frames  that's why it's important that they sit  perfectly right from the start and  anyone who knows wood knows it's  something unusual to have on your face  this is  it  nowadays these glasses are far from  unusual aviator sunglasses  originally they were made for american  military pilots but later gained cult  status and they're as wearable as ever  they differ in detail the difference is  that for ladies they have more features  so for example here you've got leather  in various colors  they're still big this year and some are  a bit more rounded  that makes them more streamlined i  for gentlemen they're a bit squarer they  usually prefer things that aren't too  playful  and another classic design the  round-shaped panto glasses of the 1920s  also this summer more and more people  are slipping on cat eye glasses or  butterfly shaped glasses the vintage  look is in  the cat eyebrows  the cat eye and butterfly glasses are  very new models and haven't been on the  market for long  any lady can wear them if she wants to  the cat eye glasses are more for narrow  faces  anyone can wear the butterfly glasses  color blocking is also a must right now  yellow purple  green or bright red the bolder the  better with color blocking anything goes  for me  i definitely like them because i have a  large head i choose a model that really  suits my face  and i like neon colors whatever's in  fashion right now  i think light colors are nice for the  summer like these that are a bit pearl  colored  they're colorful they're big they're  plastic modern but at the same time  i generally prefer sunglasses that are a  bit bigger so they cover half your face  my favorite sunglasses at the moment are  the ones i'm wearing aviator glasses i  find them really stylish  they're okay to go  for fans of the wooden variety the guys  from cowboys are already planning their  next collection alongside models in  exotic sobrano and sandalwood they'll be  turning to native germanwood for new  inspiration
 

